# Security & secrets

## API keys
- The user enters the OpenAI-compatible **base URL, API key and model** in Settings. The key is stored **only in `localStorage` on the device** (key `dt:settings`). It is never sent anywhere except as the `Authorization: Bearer` header to the user-configured base URL.
- **Never commit, log, print or echo secrets.** No `console.log` of settings, request headers or full request objects. Error messages and exports must not contain the key. Mask it in the UI (`sk-…abcd`) and add a "Clear key" button.
- Memory export/import (JSON) **excludes** settings and keys.
- **No `.env` files with real values.** Only `.env.example` with obvious placeholders is allowed. The app has no build-time secrets at all.
- Agents: never read or print `.env*`, `*.pem`, SSH keys, `~/.config/gh/hosts.yml`, `auth.json`, or env vars containing KEY/TOKEN/SECRET. Never touch `~/.hermes`. Never `git push --force`. The project hooks enforce this (`.cursor/hooks/`).

## Network & errors
- All agent calls go through one client in `src/agent/client.ts`, with a timeout (`AbortController`) and typed errors.
- Map failures to calm, plain-English messages with a next step:
  - CORS/network (`TypeError: Failed to fetch`) → "Can't reach the API from the browser. The provider may block browser requests (CORS). Check the base URL or use a provider that allows browser access."
  - 401/403 → "The API key was rejected. Check it in Settings."
  - 404 → "Model or endpoint not found. Check the base URL and model name."
  - 429 → "Rate limit reached. Wait a moment and try again."
  - Invalid JSON from the model → retry once, then fall back to the offline bank.
- When the agent is unavailable, the app keeps working fully with the built-in bank.

## Privacy
- **No telemetry, analytics, trackers, or third-party scripts/fonts/CDNs.** All data (memory, stats) stays on the device.
- Add a strict CSP `<meta>` in `index.html`: `default-src 'self'`. `connect-src` has to allow the user-chosen API origin, so document why `https:` is permitted there.
- Render model output as text/markdown with sanitisation (no raw `innerHTML` of untrusted content). KaTeX runs with `trust: false`.
